From: Try Omarchy contributors
Subject: [PATCH] darwin: the main loop runs at user-interactive QoS

What: the qemu_main thread (QEMU's main loop on macOS) asks for
QOS_CLASS_USER_INTERACTIVE; TRYOMARCHY_MAIN_LOOP_QOS=default keeps the default
QoS. QEMU's log says which one it got.

Why: the main loop feeds the sound card (the HDA DMA timer and the 1 ms
audio timer) and runs virgl. At the default QoS it competes on equal terms
with the vCPU threads and the Mac's own work; a busy guest on a busy Mac
delays it by 10-50 ms again and again, and the sound crackles. Measured on
an M4 Max, 8 vCPUs busy + glmark2 + 8 busy Mac threads, 150 s: audio timer
late 5-9 ms 4906x, 10-19 ms 825x, 20-49 ms 65x at the default QoS; 52x, 1x,
0x at user-interactive (notes: audio-crackle track).

Upstream: not sent (a Darwin policy choice; upstream leaves QoS alone).
Tested in OmacVM: QEMU's log line; the audio-crackle measurements (run.sh, analyze.py).

Adapted from OmacVM's patch of the same name (MIT,
https://github.com/gillesgoetsch/OmacVM), with its log lines and
environment variable renamed for Try Omarchy.

--- a/system/main.c
+++ b/system/main.c
@@ -39,12 +39,40 @@
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_DARWIN
 #include <CoreFoundation/CoreFoundation.h>
+#include <pthread/qos.h>
 #endif
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_DARWIN
+/*
+ * The main loop feeds the sound card (HDA DMA and the audio timer)
+ * and runs virgl. At the default QoS it competes with the vCPU threads, so a
+ * busy guest on a busy Mac delays it by tens of ms and the sound breaks up.
+ * User-interactive QoS (as the window thread) puts it first.
+ * TRYOMARCHY_MAIN_LOOP_QOS=default keeps the default.
+ */
+static void tryomarchy_main_loop_qos(void)
+{
+    const char *v = getenv("TRYOMARCHY_MAIN_LOOP_QOS");
+
+    if (v && strcmp(v, "default") == 0) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "Try Omarchy: main loop QoS: default\n");
+        return;
+    }
+    if (pthread_set_qos_class_self_np(QOS_CLASS_USER_INTERACTIVE, 0) != 0) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "Try Omarchy: main loop QoS: default (user-interactive refused)\n");
+        return;
+    }
+    fprintf(stderr, "Try Omarchy: main loop QoS: user-interactive\n");
+}
+#endif
+
 static void *qemu_default_main(void *opaque)
 {
     int status;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_DARWIN
+    tryomarchy_main_loop_qos();
+#endif
     replay_mutex_lock();
     bql_lock();
     status = qemu_main_loop();
